li-claim-mimicry : Block
li-claim-mimicry = prose (cons "**The neurotypical unit derives behavioral direction primarily by mimicry.** The typical human derives behavioral direction from the group at the cost of its own perception and judgment: Asch’s conformers, perceptual change under conformity, overimitation of what the child knows is silly, reputation-dependent giving. Autistic subjects do so far less." (cons "Avik's words: 15 Nov — inhibition is retardation; the neurotypical unit derives direction by mimicry." (cons "References: li-ref-asch, li-ref-berns-2005, li-ref-marsh-2013, li-ref-yafai-2014, li-ref-bowler-worley-1994, li-ref-izuma-2011, li-ref-lazzaro-2018." (cons "Serves: dispel-ignorance-in-neuroscience." (cons "Rendered in: the exposition (I–XII above); the notes toward the exposition (above)." nil)))))
